{
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "sigiro-www",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-07-24",
  "compatibility_flags": [
    "nodejs_compat"
  ],
  // No `main` and no `assets`. Blume finds this file at the project root and hands
  // it to `@astrojs/cloudflare` as `configPath`; the adapter then writes both keys
  // into `dist/server/wrangler.json`, and that generated file is what `bun run
  // deploy` ships. Naming an entrypoint here does not override it, it breaks the
  // build — the Cloudflare Vite plugin fails to resolve it.
  //
  // What belongs here is everything the adapter cannot know: the name, the routes,
  // and the bindings.
  //
  // The whole site, on one Worker. `sigiro.com/` is the landing page and
  // `sigiro.com/docs/*` is the docs, from one Blume app — so the `sigiro-docs`
  // Worker that served docs.sigiro.com for two days is gone, along with its custom
  // domain.
  //
  // Zone routes, not `custom_domain: true`. A custom domain makes Cloudflare own
  // the DNS record, so it refuses any hostname that already has one —
  // `Hostname 'sigiro.com' already has externally managed DNS records`. The
  // leftover proxied A records from the old Pages project are still there and
  // deleting them needs a DNS-edit credential this deploy path does not have. A
  // route needs no such thing: it intercepts the hostname at the edge ahead of
  // whatever those records point at.
  //
  // docs.sigiro.com is NOT here yet, and `src/middleware.ts` that redirects it is
  // therefore not reachable. Cloudflare's assets router answers before the Worker
  // runs, so a request to `docs.sigiro.com/quickstart` is a 404 from the asset
  // layer and the middleware never fires — verified against `wrangler dev`. The
  // knob for that is `assets.run_worker_first`, and this file cannot set it: the
  // adapter writes only `binding` and `directory` into the generated config and
  // drops everything else. It would also put every image and script through the
  // Worker, which is a poor trade for one redirect.
  //
  // So the subdomain stays on the old `sigiro-docs` Worker for now and is retired
  // separately.
  //
  // `workers_dev` is off: it published a second origin serving the identical site,
  // with our canonical tags, our sitemap and our OG tags on it.
  // `/docs/api/*` are retired-URL REDIRECTS, not content pages. Blume derives
  // `run_worker_first` from the first path segment of content routes, so
  // `/docs/reference` alone forces `/docs/*` — which swallows these redirects and
  // routes them through the Worker. There, `@astrojs/cloudflare` declares
  // `redirects: false`, so Astro defaults the status and the configured 302
  // becomes a **301** at the edge, which browsers cache more or less forever.
  // The generated `_redirects` is correct (302); it is simply never consulted.
  // Excluding them here restores the asset layer, which honours the status.
  // Verified: every path inside `run_worker_first` served 301, every path
  // outside it (`/sitemap.xml`, `/openapi.json`, `/twitter`) served 302.
  // Blume MERGES this list ahead of its own rules (`mergeRunWorkerFirstRules`),
  // and Cloudflare evaluates in order, so a leading negative wins.
  "assets": {
    "run_worker_first": ["!/docs/api/*", "!/docs/api", "/", "/docs", "/docs/*"]
  },
  "workers_dev": false,
  "routes": [
    { "pattern": "sigiro.com/*", "zone_name": "sigiro.com" },
    { "pattern": "www.sigiro.com/*", "zone_name": "sigiro.com" }
  ],
  // Release artifacts, served by the `/dl/[...key]` route that
  // `blume.config.ts` injects.
  //
  // A bucket of its own, not `sigiro-prod`. That bucket holds tenant telemetry,
  // and /dl is an unauthenticated public route: putting both behind one binding
  // means one key-handling mistake in that route is a data leak rather than a
  // 404. Two buckets make that class of bug impossible instead of unlikely.
  //
  // The bucket itself stays private. Reads go through the Worker, so there is no
  // public bucket URL and no second hostname to add.
  "r2_buckets": [{ "binding": "DOWNLOADS", "bucket_name": "sigiro-dl" }]
}
